{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Propagate.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.propagateMul\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">propagateMul</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Propagator\">Propagator</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Propagator for the `0*a`, `1*a`, `a*0`, `a*1` for semirings that do not have good support in\n`grind ring`. We need this propagator because have normalization rules for them, and users\nwere surprised when using `grind [zero_mul]` did not have any effect. In this scenario,\n`grind` was correctly instantiating `zero_mul : 0*a = 0`, but the normalizer reduces the\ninstance to `True`.\n\nAlternative approach: We improve the support for equality reasoning for non-commutative rings\nand semirings in `grind ring`. For example, we could just replace equalities and keep renormalizing.\nIf we implement this feature, this propagator can be deleted.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Propagate.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.propagateMul","kind":"def","line":111,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.propagateMul","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Propagate.lean#L111-L138"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Propagate.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.propagateNatShiftRight\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">propagateNatShiftRight</span></a> </span><span class=\